1196	/**
1197	 * Provision (or repair) the account-level scoped MySQL user for the PROPRIETARY
1198	 * in-portal DB manager. Creates `<username>_mgr`@'localhost' and grants it on
1199	 * `<username>\_%`.* ONLY — every one of THIS account's databases and nothing else
1200	 * (see buildDbMgrGrantSql for the escaped-glob isolation proof). The password was
1201	 * generated + stored encrypted by ensureDbManager; we decrypt it here to apply
1202	 * it. Idempotent (CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS + ALTER USER re-asserts the password,
1203	 * so a repair run realigns the box with the stored cred). Flips dbMgrReady=true
1204	 * so the portal can start executing queries as this user.
1205	 *
1206	 * SECURITY: the grant is db-scoped, so `ALL PRIVILEGES` confers NO global
1207	 * FILE/PROCESS/SUPER — this user can never read node files or reach a peer's
1208	 * databases or the `mysql`/system schemas. The SQL is built from validated
1209	 * identifiers and a `[A-Za-z0-9]` password, shell-escaped for `mysql -e` exactly
